  "brief": "You are helping a Strong eSIM reseller work with the Strong eSIM API.\nThis file is the complete reference: every endpoint, its method, path, parameters and example body.\nBase URL is https://api.strongesim.com/api/v1. All paths below are relative to it.\nAuthenticate first with POST /auth/login using the account in `credentials`.\nThat returns an accessToken and a session_id. Send BOTH on every authenticated call:\n  Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>\n  X-Session-ID: <session_id>\nThe access token expires after about an hour. Refresh it rather than logging in repeatedly.\nMoney is real. Orders debit the reseller's prepaid wallet and provision a real eSIM immediately.\nNever place an order, a top up or a refund without the reseller explicitly asking for that exact action.\nSend one stable idempotency key per order so a retry cannot double charge.\nIf the password below is still the placeholder, ask the reseller for it. Do not guess it.",
  "credentials": {
    "email": "info@me-sim.com",
    "password": "<your Strong eSIM password, the same one you sign in with>",
    "note": "Your password is deliberately not included. The portal never stores it, and a credential that can spend your wallet should not be uploaded to an AI provider. Fill it in locally if you need to, and remove it before sharing this file."
  },
  "auth": {
    "login": {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/login"
    },
    "headers": [
      {
        "key": "Authorization",
        "value": "Bearer {access_token}",
        "note": "JWT access token from POST /auth/login"
      },
      {
        "key": "X-Session-ID",
        "value": "{session_id}",
        "note": "Session id returned at login, tracks the session"
